g('volumetric-weight-air-freight', 'air', 'Volumetric weight|how air freight is priced',
  'How volumetric weight works in air freight, the divisor (6000 for cargo), and how chargeable weight is decided.',
  'Air cargo is priced on weight, but a bulky parcel takes space, so airlines charge the greater of the real weight and the volume weight.',
  [('The formula', 'Volume weight in kg = L × W × H in cm ÷ 6000 for most air cargo. For many express couriers the divisor is 5000.'),
   ('Example', [('table', ['Item', 'Value'], [['Carton 60 × 50 × 40 cm', '120,000 cm³'], ['Volume weight (÷ 6000)', '20 kg'], ['Actual weight', '12 kg'], ['Chargeable weight', '20 kg']])]),
   ('Whole shipment', 'Add the volume weight of all pieces, and compare it with the total actual weight. The greater is the chargeable weight.'),
   ('How to cut the cost', 'Pack tighter, remove empty space, and ship in smaller boxes if the weight is low.')],
  [('Why 6000?', 'It is the IATA standard for general cargo: six cubic metres per tonne.'),
   ('Do couriers use the same?', 'Many use 5000, so the charge is higher for bulky parcels.'),
   ('Is there a calculator?', 'Our CBM calculator and air ULD calculator show the volume.')],
  ('cbm-calculator', 'Open the CBM calculator'))
g('air-freight-chargeable-weight-and-rates', 'air', 'Air freight rates|how a quote is built',
  'How air freight rates are built: chargeable weight, weight breaks, minimum charge, fuel and security surcharges, and handling at each end.',
  'An air rate looks simple, but it has several layers. Here is how to read it.',
  [('Base rate', 'A price per kg that goes down as the weight goes up, in breaks such as under 45 kg, over 45, 100, 300 and 500 kg. There is a minimum charge per shipment.'),
   ('Surcharges', 'Fuel, security and sometimes war risk or a peak season surcharge, charged per kg.'),
   ('Handling', 'Origin handling, airline terminal charges, documentation and customs clearance at each end.'),
   ('How to compare', 'Ask for an all-in rate from airport to airport, and from door to door, with the chargeable weight shown. Check the transit time and whether it is a direct flight.')],
  [('Why is the rate per kg lower for more weight?', 'The airline gives a volume discount at set weight breaks.'),
   ('What is a minimum charge?', 'The lowest amount the airline will charge for a shipment.'),
   ('Do rates change often?', 'Yes, weekly or even daily in a tight market.')],
  ('freight-compare', 'Open the freight compare tool'))
g('air-freight-vs-sea-freight', 'air', 'Air freight vs sea freight|how to choose',
  'Air or sea? A comparison of cost, transit time, reliability, size limits and when each mode makes sense.',
  'Air is fast and costly. Sea is slow and cheap. The right choice depends on the value, the urgency and the weight.',
  [('At a glance', [('table', ['', 'Air', 'Sea'], [['Transit', 'Days', 'Weeks'], ['Cost per kg', 'High', 'Low'], ['Best for', 'Urgent, high value, perishable', 'Heavy, bulky, low value'], ['Handling', 'Less', 'More'], ['Size limit', 'Tighter', 'Wider']])]),
   ('Total cost', 'Include the stock carrying cost. A slow sea shipment ties up cash and stock for weeks. For goods with a high value per kilo, air can cost less in total.'),
   ('Hybrid', 'Sea-air through a hub such as Dubai gives a middle option. See our air-sea bridge service.'),
   ('Rule of thumb', 'Under about 100 kg and urgent, use air. Over a few cubic metres and not urgent, use sea.')],
  [('Is air freight greener?', 'No. Air has a higher carbon footprint per tonne-km.'),
   ('What about sea-air?', 'It is faster than sea and cheaper than air for some lanes.'),
   ('Can I compare quotes?', 'Yes. Our freight compare tool gives a quick view.')],
  ('freight-compare', 'Open the freight compare tool'))
g('express-courier-vs-air-freight', 'air', 'Express courier vs air freight|which is better',
  'Express courier or air freight? Differences in price, speed, limits, customs and when to switch from one to the other.',
  'Courier is door to door and quick. Air freight is cheaper for heavier loads and gives more control over customs.',
  [('Courier', ['Door to door, with tracking, in 2 to 5 days.', 'Duty paid by the courier on your behalf.', 'Weight, size and value limits.', 'Higher price per kg, because of the service.']),
   ('Air freight', ['Airport to airport or door to door, in 3 to 7 days.', 'A normal customs clearance, with a bill of entry or shipping bill.', 'Lower price per kg for weight over about 50 kg.', 'No tight limit on size and value.']),
   ('When to switch', 'Above roughly 30 to 50 kg, or for regulated goods, or for high value, air freight usually wins. For documents and samples, courier is easier.'),
   ('Customs', 'Courier customs clearance has simpler forms but limits. Air freight uses the full process with more control over the classification and the credit.')],
  [('Can a courier carry dangerous goods?', 'Only with the carrier approval and the right packing. Many lines refuse.'),
   ('Which is better for e-commerce?', 'Courier for small parcels. Consolidated air freight for large volumes.'),
   ('Which has better tracking?', 'Courier, usually. Air freight tracking follows the AWB.')],
  ('track-shipment', 'Open the tracking hub'))
g('air-cargo-uld-and-pallets-explained', 'air', 'Air cargo ULDs|pallets and containers explained',
  'What a unit load device (ULD) is in air cargo, the main types (PMC, PAG, AKE, AKH), sizes and how loading works.',
  'Air cargo is loaded into units called ULDs, either pallets with a net or containers, that fit the aircraft hold.',
  [('Main types', [('table', ['Code', 'Type'], [['PMC / PAG', 'Pallet with a net, for main deck and lower deck'], ['AKE', 'Lower deck container, LD3'], ['AKH', 'Lower deck container for narrow body aircraft'], ['LD7', 'Large lower deck container'], ['Reefer / thermal', 'Temperature controlled units']])]),
   ('How it is used', 'The forwarder builds the ULD, weighs it and gives the airline a load sheet. The airline loads it in the hold.'),
   ('Limits', 'Each aircraft type has weight and contour limits for the ULD. Tall cargo may only fit on a freighter main deck.'),
   ('Planning', 'Our air cargo ULD load calculator shows how many cartons fit a pallet or a container.')],
  [('Can I rent a whole ULD?', 'Yes, as a unit load charter or a block space, from a forwarder or an airline.'),
   ('What is a freighter?', 'An aircraft that carries only cargo, and has a main deck for large units.'),
   ('Is the ULD charged by its weight?', 'Charges are on the chargeable weight of the cargo, with a minimum for the ULD in some tariffs.')],
  ('air-cargo-uld-load-calculator', 'Open the ULD load calculator'))
g('air-freight-booking-steps', 'air', 'How to book an air shipment|step by step',
  'How to book an air freight shipment from India: quote, booking, packing, documents, customs and tracking.',
  'Air freight moves fast, so the steps need to go in order and on time.',
  [('Before you book', ['Get the weight and the dimensions of the packed cargo.', 'Confirm the Incoterm and who handles each end.', 'Check the product for restrictions: dangerous goods, batteries, perishables.']),
   ('Booking', ['Ask for quotes with the chargeable weight and the all-in price.', 'Confirm the flight or the service level, and the cut-off.', 'Send the shipping instructions and the documents: invoice, packing list, certificates.']),
   ('Customs and flight', ['Your broker files the shipping bill and gets a let export order.', 'The cargo is handed to the airline terminal and screened.', 'The airline issues the AWB and flies the cargo.']),
   ('At destination', 'The consignee gets the arrival notice, files the import documents and pays the duty. Use the AWB number to track.')],
  [('How early do I need to deliver?', 'Usually several hours before departure. Ask for the cut-off for the flight.'),
   ('Is there a size limit?', 'Yes, for the aircraft door and the deck type.'),
   ('Can I book without a forwarder?', 'Airlines sell to agents. For most shippers a forwarder is needed.')],
  ('awb-label-generator', 'Open the AWB label generator'))
g('perishable-cargo-by-air-and-sea', 'air', 'Shipping perishables|temperature, speed and paperwork',
  'How to ship perishable cargo such as fruit, vegetables, fish and flowers by air or sea: packing, cold chain and certificates.',
  'For perishables, time and temperature decide the outcome. The best packaging cannot make up for a break in the cold chain.',
  [('Choose the mode', 'Air for the most delicate and short shelf life items. Reefer containers by sea for fruit and vegetables that last weeks.'),
   ('Pack and pre-cool', ['Cool the product before loading.', 'Use packaging made for the product and the transit time.', 'Add gel packs, dry ice or liners as the airline and the cargo need.']),
   ('Paperwork', 'Phytosanitary or health certificates, export registration with APEDA or MPEDA where needed, and the commercial invoice and AWB or BL.'),
   ('Cold chain', 'Book with a forwarder who can arrange cold storage at the airport or port, and ask for the temperature data after arrival.')],
  [('Is dry ice allowed?', 'Yes, as a class 9 item with the right marking and limits.'),
   ('How long can the cargo wait?', 'It depends on the product. Ask for the shelf life and plan the cut-off to leave a margin.'),
   ('Who is liable for spoilage?', 'Carrier liability is limited. Cargo insurance for perishables needs special cover.')],
  ('perishables', 'See our perishables service'))
